0328-negroni-wlan-htt-dp: Wi-Fi, the HTT data path (ath11k dp/hal for WCN6855, polled), 802.3 frames both ways.
negroni_wlan_dp.c: common rings + one link-descriptor bank + REO routing/aging + DSCP maps after the CE rings
(ath11k_dp_alloc), REO2SW1..4 before WMI INIT, HTT version + LMAC rings (rx refill, 2 mac buf, 2 rxdma error,
2 monitor status) + rx buffers + HTT SRING_SETUP + monitor filter off after WMI READY; per peer HTT PEER_MAP,
default routing, 17 REO queues (WMI reorder queue setup), vdev TX encap / RX decap Ethernet; TX by TCL data ring 0
(completions WBM2SW0), RX from REO2SW (Ethernet decap, native-Wi-Fi converted), error rings recycle buffers and
return link descriptors; API negroni_wlan_tx queue (64) and the RX callback; EAPOL kept for 0329. CE4 (HTT out) in
negroni_wlan_ce.c, windowed register helpers; HTT hooks in negroni_wlan_wmi.c; boot-arg negroniwlan_dp=0 skips it.
Every device address via negroni_wlan_dma_alloc. Details: patches/xnu/README-wifi.md "0328".

